--TEST--
`Core\Db\Queryable` is a type and nothing more: a program's own class may not implement it, and `as Core\Db\Queryable` is not a checked conversion — `rule:core-classes/db-transactions`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// A program's own class cannot implement the interface: the members of
// `Core\Db\Queryable` read a connection's handle off their receiver, and this
// class has none.
class Fake implements Core\Db\Queryable {
}

// No value is ever an instance of the interface itself, so there is no
// checked conversion into it. `is` is the way to ask.
mixed $m = 1;
var $q = $m as Core\Db\Queryable;
--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0328]: `Core\Db\Queryable` is implemented only by `Core` classes
%a
error[E0711]: `mixed` cannot be converted to `Core\Db\Queryable`
%a
error: aborting due to 2 errors
%a
